[x] Emit canonical index IDs as a line stream =index-ids-format $DONE 2026-08-08. Added graphd --format ids for every index view, emitting each canonical id binding unchanged as one line in SPARQL query order; empty views emit zero bytes. Other query families reject the index-only format. Documented the projection contract and verified exact ordered URNs, empty output, real-workspace output, full graphd tests, strict Clippy, formatting, doctests, diagnostics, and diff checks.$ !1 %2026-08-08T19:40 #019fe446-ad2d-7fd2-b938-eb4190114be9
[x] Capture the exact existing index JSON contract =index-json-contract $DONE 2026-08-15. Published specifications/schemas/index_query_result.schema.json (Draft 2020-12): ordered array of index-family rows with required id, name, status, source_file, source_line, charter_root and optional priority, parent/parent_name, scheduled_at, due_date. status enum is the full 5-state domain (shape not membership); additionalProperties false; strict urn:uuid pattern on id/parent; parent<->parent_name co-required. Validated the schema and graphd real bytes for default, unscheduled, and weekly views; scheduled_at/due_date serialization confirmed as xsd:dateTime lexical from graphd tests.$ !1 %2026-08-15T12:09 #019fdffc-b160-74f1-a8b3-a3a5694e794e
[x] Add transaction request and result schemas with fixtures =transaction-schemas $DONE 2026-08-15. Published specifications/schemas/transaction_request.schema.json and transaction_result.schema.json (Draft 2020-12) + fixtures under specifications/examples/transactions/ (valid_multi_op, invalid_empty_set, invalid_unknown_op; committed, dry_run, rejected_not_found, invalid_updated_with_children). Request: ordered operations oneOf update-action/complete-action/cancel-action targeting urn:uuid; set mirrors core ActionUpdate scalar surface (name/description/priority/context/alias/state/scheduled_at/duration), state serialized snake_case with terminal values rejected by core guard, predecessors/is_sequential deferred. Result: kind-discriminated committed/dry-run/rejected reusing clearhead-cli VerbOutcome (children=cascade count) and VerbError (not-found/ambiguous/already-closed) verbatim; no CAS/conflict in v1. All schemas validate as 2020-12; valid fixtures pass, invalid fixtures reject for the right reasons.$ !1 %2026-08-15T12:37 <index-json-contract #019fdffc-b169-7d32-95af-b3e73d0a1412
[x] Validate producer bytes against the schemas =schema-producer-tests $DONE 2026-08-15 (index-producer scope). Added clearhead-graphd/tests/spec_conformance.rs behind a new spec-conformance feature: seeds a workspace exercising every optional column (parent/parent_name/priority via unscheduled, scheduled_at/due_date via agenda) and validates real index JSON for default/unscheduled/agenda/weekly against specifications/schemas/index_query_result.schema.json via CLEARHEAD_SPEC_DIR. Includes a negative test proving the validator has teeth, and keeps bare cargo test standalone. Wired into scripts/validate-pinned alongside the Core block. Rust jsonschema 0.18 enforces Draft 2020-12 cleanly. Transaction-RESULT producer-byte conformance is intentionally NOT here: it lives in the transact leg done gate (receipts validate against transaction_result.schema.json), which is gated on durable-verbs.$ !1 %2026-08-15T12:46 <transaction-schemas #019fdffc-b172-7153-a823-e9d67c81f18e
